      {
       "path": "Plans/Contracts_V0.md",
       "unit": "CV-3100",
       "line_start": 55286,
       "line_end": 55286,
       "quote": "Newly authored owner contract under DL-045, written for DL-080 option 1 (PNC-019 lane rv8b, 2026-11-14). goal_run.replanned binds schema ID pm.goal_runtime_event.goal_run_replanned.schema.v3 at Plans/event_payloads/goal_runtime/goal_run_replanned.v3.schema.json, closed at the root (additionalProperties false, unevaluatedProperties false) and self-contained, on the GoalRun envelope grammar that CV-288 keeps for Event Authority custody after DL-478: expected_goal_run_revision, goal_run_revision and idempotency_key are required; expected_goal_revision and parent_goal_id are gone; goal_revision is the unchanged Goal context revision; execution_role is runtime_controller. The specific payload keeps the seven v2 fields (goal_run_id, previous_workgraph_ref, new_workgraph_ref, replan_generation with maximum 4294967295, affected_worknode_refs, cancelled_or_resteered_refs, next_action) and adds the required original_graph_patch and original_graph_patch_history from the accepted v8 source, whose graph-patch and OwnerIdentity definitions are inlined under graph_patch_* with their grammar unchanged. It is the restriction successor of the v8 draft clock-split payload (Plans/goal_run_replan_contracts/payload-correspondence.json): each canon instance maps to exactly one draft instance that satisfies the draft's own owner rules, and back; no other draft instance has a canon image. The delivery profile pm.goal_run_replanned.delivery.v3 selects this schema for the v8 Replan writer's WholeProducerSubmission and appended Event (adoption correction C1). The whole v2 schema stays unchanged as the historical reader and is never reinterpreted. Prepared without admission: the registry row keeps v2 until the S5b switch (prepared row in Plans/goal_run_replan_contracts/prepared-registry-row.json)."
      }
     ],
     "finding": "The registry now equals RV8B's exact prepared v3 row, resolving the source grade's sole pending selector prerequisite."
    }
   }
